.SH "NAME"
gfarm-pcp \- copy files to multiple hosts
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR\ 'u
\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIsource\fR \fIdestination\fR
.HP \w'\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR\ 'u
\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIsource\fR... \fIdirectory\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR
copies local files
\fIsource\fR
to
\fIdestination\fR
or
\fIdirectory\fR
on each host listed in a hostfile, by using a remote copy command,
\fBscp \-pr\fR
by default\&. A relative path of the destination is relative to the home directory on the remote host\&. It is useful, for example, to distribute configuration files to filesystem nodes of Gfarm\&.
.PP
By default, files are copied to one host after another\&. When the \-p option is specified, files are copied to multiple hosts in parallel\&.
.PP
The format of the hostfile, and how the local host is skipped, are the same as
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR\&. See
\fBgfarm-prun\fR(1)\&.
.PP
When the PRUN_RCP environment variable is set to
no, files are copied by the remote shell command specified by the PRUN_RSH environment variable, without a remote copy command\&. In this case, the last argument must be a directory on the remote host, and only regular files can be copied\&. The permission of the files is not preserved\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-a\fR
.RS 4
Copies files also to the local host, if it is listed in the hostfile\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR \fIhostfile\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a hostfile\&. If `\-\*(Aq is specified, the list of hosts is read from the standard input\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-m\fR \fImax_jobs\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the maximum number of hosts to which files are copied in parallel with the \-p option\&. The default is 16\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-n\fR
.RS 4
Displays the commands that would be executed, but does not execute them\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-p\fR
.RS 4
Copies files to multiple hosts in parallel in the background\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-rcp\fR \fIrcp_command\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a remote copy command\&. The default is
\fBscp \-pr\fR\&. If
no
is specified, files are copied by the remote shell command as described above\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v\fR
.RS 4
Displays the host name before copying files to the host\&. This option has no effect with the \-p option\&.
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.PP
\fBPRUN_RCP\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a remote copy command\&. The default is
\fBscp \-pr\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_RSH\fR
.RS 4
Specifies a remote shell command that is used when PRUN_RCP is
no\&. The default is
\fBssh\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPRUN_HOSTFILE\fR, \fBPRUN_HOSTNAME\fR, \fBPRUN_MAX_JOBS\fR, \fBPRUN_PARALLEL\fR, \fBPRUN_ALL_INCLUDE_MYSELF\fR, \fBPRUN_VERBOSE\fR
.RS 4
The same as
\fBgfarm\-prun\fR\&. See
\fBgfarm-prun\fR(1)\&.
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
\fBgfarm\-pcp\fR
exits with 0 when files are copied to all hosts successfully\&. Otherwise, it exits with the exit status of the copy command for a host to which the copy fails\&. When it fails for two or more hosts, the exit status for one of them is returned\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Copies
gfarm2\&.conf
to
/tmp
on all hosts listed in
$HOME/\&.nodelist, except the local host\&.
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
	$ gfarm\-pcp gfarm2\&.conf /tmp
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
Copies the shared secret key of the user to the home directory on all hosts listed in
hosts, in parallel\&.
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
	$ gfarm\-pcp \-p \-h hosts \&.gfarm_shared_key \&.
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.SH "FILES"
.PP
$HOME/\&.nodelist
.RS 4
the default hostfile
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBgfarm-prun\fR(1),
\fBscp\fR(1)
